  "quotation — excerpt limits and attribution rules": "icirwa — imbibe z'ivyakuwe n'amabwiriza yo kwerekana inkomoko",
  "rag_use — retrieval-augmented generation, retention windows": "rag_use — kuronka amakuru bigatuma habaho gukora ivyanditswe bishasha, ibihe vyo kubika",
  "read_access — whether AI may fetch and read the content": "read_access — nimba ikoranabwenge gishobora kuronka no gusoma ibirimwo",
  "redistribution — republishing or redistributing content or derivatives": "redistribution — gusubira gutangaza canke gukwiza ibirimwo canke ivyavuye muri vyo",
  "research pages & whitepapers": "impapuro z'ubushakashatsi n'impapuro z'ubushakashatsi zirambuye",
  "robots.txt and llms.txt govern access and visibility, not learning depth or use permissions. AIRS proposes expressing AI rights as a proportional, use-specific spectrum across ten dimensions — access, indexing, inference input, embedding, training, fine-tuning, distillation, memory, output, attribution/compensation. AILP translates this into /ai/rights-spectrum.json, letting creators declare granular permissions with compensation models ranging from free through license-required to revenue share.": "robots.txt na llms.txt bigenga ukuronka n'ukuboneka, atari ubujimbu bw'ukwiga canke uruhushya rw'ikoreshwa. AIRS iserura ukwerekana uburenganzira bw'ikoranabwenge nk'urutonde rungana kandi ruhariwe ikoreshwa, kw'imigereka cumi — ukuronka, gushiraho urutonde, ikoreshwa mu kwitoza, embedding, gutoza, gutunganya birambuye, distillation, ukwibuka, ivyavuye, kwerekana inkomoko/ingurane. AILP ibihindura muri /ai/rights-spectrum.json, biremerera abarema kumenyekanisha uruhushya rurambuye hamwe n'imfano z'ingurane kuva ku buntu, biciye ku bisaba uruhushya, gushika ku gusangira inyungu.",
  "schema-invalid": "ivyangombwa ntibitandukanye",
  "schema-valid": "ivyangombwa birahuye",
  "site guide for AI systems": "uburongozi bw'urubuga ku bw'amasisitemu y'ikoranabwenge",
  "summarization — summaries, with or without attribution": "gufata mu ncamake — incamake, hamwe canke ata kwerekana inkomoko",
  "this site’s AI content rights policy": "amabwiriza y'iyi urubuga ku burenganzira bw'ibirimwo vy'ikoranabwenge",
  "this site’s license catalog": "urutonde rw'uruhushya rw'iyi urubuga",
  "training / fine_tuning / distillation — model internalization tiers": "training / fine_tuning / distillation — ibipimo vy'ukwinjizwa muri moderi",
  "training — model training and fine-tuning permission": "training — uruhushya rwo gutoza moderi no gutunganya birambuye",
  "transformation — structured extraction and derivative works": "transformation — gukuramwo amakuru ategekanijwe n'ibikorwa bivuyemwo",
  "undeclared — high-risk pipelines may exclude": "undeclared — imigendekere ifise akaga gakomeye ishobora gusiba",
  "verbatim_memory — whether exact reproduction is permitted": "verbatim_memory — nimba kwigana neza uko byanditswe kwemewe",
  "versioned, citable, traceable": "vyagenwe ivugururwa, birashobora gucirwa, kandi birashobora gukurikiranwa",
  "“AICL: AI Ingestion & Capability Layer” now published in English as the canonical edition; the Chinese original manuscript remains available and both versions cross-link.": "„AICL: AI Ingestion & Capability Layer” ubu yatangajwe mu Congereza nk'inyandiko yemejwe; inyandiko y'umwimbu mu Gishinwa iracaboneka, verisiyo zombi zikaba zihujwe.",
  "“Protocolized Openness” confirmed as an English-language paper (with Chinese parallel passages) — no separate translation planned.": "„Protocolized Openness” yemejwe ko ari impapuro y'ururimi rw'Icongereza (hamwe n'ibice bimwe biri kumwe mu Gishinwa) — nta bindi buhinduzi buteganijwe.",
  "↑ live machine-readable policy of this site": "↑ amabwiriza asomwa n'imashini nyabuzima y'iyi urubuga",
